DESCRIPTION:BI SIG Integration Services Focus Group Presents:\nIntro to SSI
	S Custom Component Development\nSpeaker: Anthony Dangelo \nMay 12th 12:00p
	m ET\nTopic Description: You have tried so hard not to write code inside o
	f SSIS\, but the day has arrived when you tired of writing the same script
	 task over and over again. Don't fret creating a Custom Component is not a
	s daunting as you might think. This session will integrate your logic with
	 SSIS Components: variables\, pipeline\, and events. This session will exp
	lore the design-time and run-time events\, the difference between Synchron
	ous and Asynchronous Components\, and debugging techniques.\n \n\nNotes  \
	nBlythe Morrow has invited you to attend an online meeting using Live Meet
	ing. Join the meeting. <https://owa.sqlpass.org/owa/redir.aspx?URL=https%3
	a%2f%2fwww.livemeeting.com%2fcc%2fusergroups%2fjoin%3fid%3d69RDJ4%26role%3
	dattend>  \n\nAudio Information \nTelephone conferencing\nUse the informat
	ion below to connect: \nToll-free: +1 (866) 379-8990 \nParticipant code: 6
	489756 \nFirst Time Users: \nTo save time before the meeting\, check your 
	system  <https://owa.sqlpass.org/owa/redir.aspx?URL=http%3a%2f%2fgo.micros
	oft.com%2ffwlink%2f%3fLinkId%3d90703> to make sure it is ready to use Micr
	osoft Office Live Meeting. \nTroubleshooting\nUnable to join the meeting? 
	Follow these steps: \n1.	Copy this address and paste it into your web brow
	ser: \nhttps://www.livemeeting.com/cc/usergroups/join <https://owa.sqlpass
	.org/owa/redir.aspx?URL=https%3a%2f%2fwww.livemeeting.com%2fcc%2fusergroup
	s%2fjoin>  \n2.	Copy and paste the required information: \nMeeting ID: 69R
	DJ4 \nLocation: https://www.livemeeting.com/cc/usergroups <https://owa.sql
	pass.org/owa/redir.aspx?URL=https%3a%2f%2fwww.livemeeting.com%2fcc%2fuserg
	roups>  \nIf you still cannot enter the meeting\, contact support <https:/
	/owa.sqlpass.org/owa/redir.aspx?URL=http%3a%2f%2fr.office.microsoft.com%2f
	r%2frlidLiveMeeting%3fp1%3d12%26p2%3den_US%26p3%3dLMInfo%26p4%3dsupport> \
	n\nNotice \nMicrosoft Office Live Meeting can be used to record meetings. 
	By participating in this meeting\, you agree that your communications may 
	be monitored or recorded at any time during the meeting. \n\n
